# In 1800, how many children died before their fifth birthday?
subtitle: "Guess how many children in a hundred died before age five in 1800, then see today's rate and how the best of then compares with the worst of now."
tags: ["health","history","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Then vs now\" note \"Guess first\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Charon | a warm, clear quiz host who loves a good fact; patient, natural pace","take":"lines"}

## In 1800, how many children died before their fifth birthday?
use: bar_chart
with:
    labels:
      - World 1800
      - World 2024
      - Norway 1850
      - Nigeria 2024
    values:
      - 43
      - 4
      - 17
      - 12
    value_labels: true
    ylim:
      - 0
      - 100
    bar_colors: same
    icons:
      - {of: globe showing europe-africa, set: twemoji}
      - {of: globe showing europe-africa, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag norway, set: twemoji}
      - {of: flag nigeria, set: twemoji}
    label_size: 32
sources:
    - id: owid_cm
      title: Child mortality rate
      authors: Our World in Data, from Gapminder (2015) and the UN Inter-agency Group for Child Mortality Estimation (2025)
      year: 2025
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/child-mortality
      finding: 'share of children dying before age five: world 42.8 % in 1800 and 3.7 % in 2024; Norway 16.8 % in 1850 (the lowest on record that year); Nigeria 11.6 % in 2024 (the highest that year) (rounded on the chart to 43, 4, 17 and 12)'
    - id: owid_deaths
      title: Number of child deaths
      authors: Our World in Data, from the UN Inter-agency Group for Child Mortality Estimation (2025)
      year: 2025
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/number-of-child-deaths-igme
      finding: about 4.86 million children died before age five in 2024
    - id: owid_article
      title: Child and Infant Mortality
      authors: Saloni Dattani, Fiona Spooner, Hannah Ritchie and Max Roser
      year: 2023
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/child-mortality
      finding: two centuries ago around half of all children died before the end of puberty

    card title "1800: how many children died young?"

In 1800, out of every hundred children born, how many died before their fifth birthday?
    draw axes

    ask "Drag the 1800 bar to your guess." on bar_1 store g default "15"
        right: Close. It was about forty-three in a hundred.
        wrong: It was about forty-three: more than four children in every ten.

So in a family with six children, losing one or more was the rule, not the exception.
    highlight bar_1

Now look at the world today: about four in a hundred.
    draw bar_2

That is a fall of more than ten times, thanks to clean water, vaccines, better food and medicine.
    arrow fall_ar #2f6b8f from.x 300 from.y 445 to.x 425 to.y 295 style.stroke_width 4
    text fall "÷ 11" #2f6b8f cites ["owid_cm"] x 450 y 390 font_size 64

It is still about five million young children a year, so the work is not done.
    text still "still 4.9 m a year" #5e584e cites ["owid_deaths"] x 470 y 500 font_size 40

Was that only the poorest places? No. Even the luckiest country of 1850, Norway, lost about seventeen children in a hundred.
    draw bar_3

And today, the hardest-hit country is Nigeria, at about twelve in a hundred.
    draw bar_4

Now put those two side by side.
    text gt ">" #b5482e cites ["owid_cm"] x 686 y 300 font_size 90

A child born in the best place of 1850 had worse odds than a child born in the worst place today.
    text payoff "best then > worst now" #b5482e cites ["owid_cm"] x 690 y 600 font_size 50

